Mode: Project

Purpose:
  Defines project mode — whether project is greenfield, brownfield,
  or hybrid.

Owns: ./

Modes:
  GREENFIELD  — new project, no existing code
  BROWNFIELD  — existing project being analyzed
  HYBRID      — mix of new and existing

Fields:
  Mode:              <GREENFIELD|BROWNFIELD|HYBRID>
  Reason:            <why this mode>
  DiscoveryStatus:
    Status:          <PENDING|IN_PROGRESS|COMPLETE>
    Timestamp:       <ISO-8601>
    Score:           <percentage>
    Unknown:         <percentage>
  DiscoveredStack:   [<technologies>]
  DiscoveredArchitecture: <style>
  DiscoveredDomains: [<domains>]
  DiscoveredTests:   [<test-types>]
  DiscoveredSecurity: [<controls>]
  DiscoveredInfrastructure: [<infra>]
  Gaps:              [<missing-items>]

Navigation:
  ProjectMode: @project/mode.sdd
  RootMode: @../mode.sdd

State: +

Note:
  This file is the project-specific mode declaration. Concrete mode
  data is generated per project by the project-structure skill.
